# Error Handling Guide

This repository does **not** use a single global `AppError`. Instead, it follows a layered approach:

- **Domain errors** live in `crates/keydock-domain` (pure validation/invariants, no IO/HTTP semantics).
- **Use case errors** live in `crates/keydock-usecase` (orchestration + domain delegation).
- **Storage/IO errors** live close to the adapter (`crates/keydock-fjall`, etc.).
- **HTTP error mapping** lives at the boundary in `crates/keydock-http` (Axum `IntoResponse`).

The goal is the same as the “single AppError methodology”, but implemented in a way that matches this codebase:
typed errors per layer, and a **single mapping point** at the transport boundary.

## Quick Start: Common Patterns (Copy-Paste Ready)

### Domain validation (pure, typed, no HTTP)

```rust
use keydock_domain::DomainError;

pub fn validate_bucket_id(raw: &str) -> Result<(), DomainError> {
    if raw.is_empty() {
        return Err(DomainError::InvalidBucketId(raw.to_string()));
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

### Use case errors wrap domain errors via `#[from]`

`crates/keydock-usecase/src/error.rs` already models this pattern:

```rust
use keydock_usecase::UseCaseError;

pub fn do_something_that_can_fail() -> Result<(), UseCaseError> {
    // Any `DomainError` can be returned with `?` and becomes `UseCaseError::Domain`.
    Ok(())
}
```

### HTTP boundary maps errors to status + JSON body

`crates/keydock-http/src/error.rs` defines the JSON shape:

```rust
#[derive(Debug, serde::Serialize)]
pub struct ErrorBody {
    pub error: String,
}
```

## Decision Guide: where should this error live?

| Situation                        | Layer to model it     | Example type                                                                            | Suggested HTTP status |
| -------------------------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |
| Input/validation violated        | Domain                | `keydock_domain::DomainError`                                                           | 400                   |
| Feature not implemented yet      | Use case or HTTP edge | `keydock_usecase::UseCaseError::NotImplemented` or `crate::error::not_implemented(...)` | 501                   |
| Storage adapter failure          | Adapter               | `keydock_fjall::FjallError`                                                             | 500                   |
| Unexpected bug / invariant break | Closest layer         | layer error enum + log                                                                  | 500 (generic message) |

## Mandatory Checklist (production-safe defaults)

- [ ] ❌ **NO** `unwrap()` or `expect()` in production code
  - ✅ Exceptions already used in this repo: tests and a few “must hold” startup defaults (e.g. default listen address parsing).
- [ ] ✅ Prefer `thiserror` + `#[from]` for transparent conversions across layers.
- [ ] ✅ Use `?` for propagation; only use `map_err` when changing error types intentionally.
- [ ] ✅ Keep domain/usecase errors free of HTTP types (`StatusCode`, `Response`, `IntoResponse`).
- [ ] ✅ Map to HTTP responses **only** in `crates/keydock-http` (single conversion point).

